wa_logger mobile

The WhatsApp Web integration (app/src/main/assets/walm-bridge.js) contains code adapted from whatsapp-web.js
(https://github.com/wwebjs/whatsapp-web.js), version 1.34.7:
  - src/Client.js (inject, requestPairingCode, attachEventListeners, setDeviceName)
  - src/util/Injected/Utils.js (injectToFunction, getMessageModel, getChat)
  - src/util/Injected/AuthStore/AuthStore.js
whatsapp-web.js is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy is in
third_party/whatsapp-web.js/LICENSE. The adapted code was rewritten for a WebView message port (no Puppeteer) and
changed in the ways described in ARCHITECTURE.md §4.

The user interface, data model and encryption design come from wa_logger (https://github.com/revocx35/wa_logger),
by the same author.
